OneiOS take18, userland/metal/patches/NativeMetal/0003: the render server counts a video surface in use only while a
command buffer that reads it runs.
Upstream: Droid-VM/macOS-DroidVM 4f77b11 (lateautumn233, 2026-11-13: compositor surface use from commit to GPU
completion) and Droid-VM/NativeMetal 43f78ae (HuJK, 2026-11-15: commandUse for 4:2:0 YCbCr surface textures in
WindowServer); 935c468 keeps the per-command-buffer count to macOS and in-place video. Adapted for iOS's render server.
What: in backboardd, a texture over a two-plane surface whose second plane's elements are twice the first's (two-plane
YCbCr, 8 or 10 bit, whatever format the texture reads it as) is commandUse: its surface is IOSurfaceIncrementUseCount'ed at
each commit of a command buffer that uses it (on the caller's thread) and decremented at that command buffer's completion
or local refusal, instead of counted for the texture's life. A view of such a texture is commandUse too. Every other
surface texture keeps the life count (an app's Core Animation draws into a backing store in place only while it is not in
use: Settings showed torn labels without it). The four interface and countUse lines the base's
build-adreno-metal-plugin.py writes are left as they are (it finds them applied); the property is a class extension.
Why: take17, YouTube at 1080p: backboardd's GPU blobs reached 1885 of its 2048 MiB with 9,399 "texture over surface
refused: OutOfMemory(Device)" and the picture went black. A decoder's or CAImageQueue's pool takes back only surfaces not
in use; counted for the texture's life, none came back while backboardd kept their textures, and VideoToolbox made more.
Switch: boot argument oneios-surface-use=video (default) | all (every surface texture of the render server, macOS-DroidVM
4f77b11's rule, an A/B: it may bring the torn labels back) | life (as before) (ONEIOS_SURFACE_USE). Removable: yes
(ONEIOS_METAL_SKIP=surface-use-while-commands-read). Works with or without metal2vulkan 0001 (the planes alone).
iOS's log: "native-metal: surface texture WxH format F over a '420v' surface: in use while a command buffer reads it" (the
first four in backboardd).

